IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crtpa-nouns`
IMPORT `crtpa-s4-defences`

-- Tests for section 4.  Every expected value is written from the text of s 4, with the reason beside it,
-- before the module was run.  In each call the inputs are, in order, those of the rule's GIVEN.

§ `Tests -- s 4(1) and (5)`

-- (1): "apply where proceedings ... are brought by a third party in reliance on section 2".
#ASSERT `s 4(1) subsections (2) to (5) apply` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) subsections (2) to (5) apply` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5): "subject to any express term of the contract as to the matters that are not to be available".
#ASSERT `s 4(5) subsections (2) and (4) are subject to an express term of the contract that takes the matter away` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(5) subsections (2) and (4) are subject to an express term of the contract that takes the matter away` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 4(2)`

-- inputs: (1) applies; (a) arises from or in connection with the contract and is relevant to the term; (b) would have been
-- available against the promisee; an express term takes the matter away.
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- either limb missing: this subsection gives the promisor no defence on these facts (JUST FALSE, marginal reading M8; the same answer as s 4(3)'s unmet "if").
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an express term takes the matter away (subsection (5)); a matter the subsection does not cover gets no defence from it.
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1) does not apply: the grant of (2) is not in play.
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 4(3)`

-- inputs: (1) applies; an express term provides for it to be available; (b) would have been available against the promisee.
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off because an express term provides for it` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "if (a) ... and (b) ...": a failed limb is the text's no for this subsection.
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off because an express term provides for it` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off because an express term provides for it` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off because an express term provides for it` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off because an express term provides for it` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 4(4)`

-- (a), inputs: (1) applies; would have been available by defence or set-off against the third party as a party; an express term takes it away.
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(a) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off as it would have been against a party` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(a) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off as it would have been against a party` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(a) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off as it would have been against a party` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(a) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off as it would have been against a party` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(a) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off as it would have been against a party` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(a) the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off as it would have been against a party` NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b), inputs: (1) applies; the matter does not arise from the contract; would have been available by counterclaim as against a party; an express term takes it away.
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(b) the matter is available to the promisor by way of counterclaim as it would have been against a party` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(b) the matter is available to the promisor by way of counterclaim as it would have been against a party` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(b) the matter is available to the promisor by way of counterclaim as it would have been against a party` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(b) the matter is available to the promisor by way of counterclaim as it would have been against a party` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(b) the matter is available to the promisor by way of counterclaim as it would have been against a party` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(b) the matter is available to the promisor by way of counterclaim as it would have been against a party` NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 4(2), (3) and (4)(a) taken together`

-- inputs: proceedings by a third party in reliance on s 2; (2)(a); (2)(b)/(3)(b); express term provides for it (3)(a);
-- would have been available against the third party as a party (4)(a); an express term takes the matter away (5).
-- (2) alone.
#ASSERT `s 4(2), (3) and (4)(a) taken together the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (3) alone.
#ASSERT `s 4(2), (3) and (4)(a) taken together the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (4)(a) alone.
#ASSERT `s 4(2), (3) and (4)(a) taken together the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2) taken away by an express term, but (3) still gives it.
#ASSERT `s 4(2), (3) and (4)(a) taken together the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- none of the three gives it: each of (2), (3) and (4)(a) gives the promisor no defence on these facts, so JUST FALSE (not "the promisor has no defence at all").
#ASSERT `s 4(2), (3) and (4)(a) taken together the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) and (4)(a) taken away by an express term and (3) not made out: every route says no.
#ASSERT `s 4(2), (3) and (4)(a) taken together the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not proceedings by a third party in reliance on s 2: (1) fails, so no route applies.
#ASSERT `s 4(2), (3) and (4)(a) taken together the matter is available to the promisor by way of defence or set-off` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 4(6)`

-- inputs: proceedings are brought against the third party; the third party seeks to enforce in reliance on s 2; could not have done so as a party.
#ASSERT `s 4(6) the third party may not enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(6) the third party may not enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(6) the third party may not enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(6) the third party may not enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(6) the third party may not enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(6) the third party may not enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Assertions on the regulative rule where nothing stands (FULFILLED)`

-- A DEONTIC value can be compared in an #ASSERT on this binary only when it is FULFILLED (probed 2026-11-05): the outcomes with a
-- standing prohibition are the traces below, read by eye.
-- the third party could have enforced the term as a party: no prohibition.
#ASSERT `s 4(6) the third party SHANT enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- no proceedings are brought against the third party: s 4(6)'s "where" is unmet.
#ASSERT `s 4(6) the third party SHANT enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS FULFILLED

§ `Traces -- the regulative rule (read by eye)`

-- the third party could not have enforced it as a party: the third party SHANT; doing it at time 2 is a breach.
#TRACE `s 4(6) the third party SHANT enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the third party` DOES `enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` AT 2
-- the third party could have enforced it as a party: no prohibition, so fulfilled.
#TRACE `s 4(6) the third party SHANT enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the third party` DOES `enforce the term in proceedings brought against the third party` AT 2
